## ❌ MISSING / NOT IMPLEMENTED

### Critical gaps
1. **`/public/og-image.jpg`** — referenced in `__root.tsx` meta but the file does not exist. Social sharing previews show a broken image.
2. **`supabase/migrations/`** — there are no migration SQL files in the `supabase/` directory. The schema exists only in the remote Supabase project; there is nothing local to recreate it.
3. **No database seeding** — no seed data for `restaurant_settings`, categories, products. A fresh deploy starts with an empty app and the customer-facing pages render nothing.
4. **`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`** missing from `.env` — `client.server.ts` presumably reads this from env but it is not in the `.env` file. Server functions (`placeOrder`, `updateOrderStatus`, etc.) will fail unless this is set in the deployment environment.
5. **`WHATSAPP_TOKEN` / `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`** env vars** — WhatsApp silently no-ops without these or the `app_config` row.

### Frontend gaps vs. README requirements
6. **Customer profile page** — README specifies a customer dashboard (name, phone, visits, reward points, favourite food, order history, saved addresses, birthday). Only order history exists via `/my-orders` (OTP-gated). No editable profile UI.
7. **PDF bill download** — `window.print()` is used for printing but there is no client-side PDF generation (no jsPDF or similar). README requires a downloadable PDF bill.
8. **Image upload for products/categories** — Admin menu form only has an "Image URL" text input. No `<input type="file">` / Cloudinary / Supabase Storage upload. Owner cannot upload a photo without an external URL.
9. **Logo and banner upload** in settings — `logo_url` and `banner_url` fields exist in `RestaurantSettings` but the settings form only exposes text inputs for the listed `FIELDS` array; `logo_url` and `banner_url` are NOT in the `FIELDS` array, so they cannot be changed from the UI at all.
10. **Theme switcher** — `theme` field exists in `restaurant_settings` and in the type but there is no UI to change it and no logic to apply different themes. Only dark mode exists.
11. **Reviews management in admin** — Reviews are read from Supabase and shown on the homepage, but there is no admin panel to approve/publish/delete reviews or for customers to submit reviews.
12. **BOGO / Combo discount types** — README lists "Buy One Get One" and "Combo Discount" types; the discount engine only handles `flat` and `percent` types (line 96 in `orders.functions.ts`). No BOGO logic.
13. **Happy Hour / Lunch / Weekend offer logic on products** — time/date filtering exists in the discount engine but the category/product targeting (`category_ids`, `product_ids` arrays in `Discount`) is never filtered server-side. Any active discount applies to the full order regardless of which products are in the cart.
14. **Discount usage counter** — `usage_count` column exists in `discounts` but is never incremented when a coupon/discount is applied.
15. **Inventory deduction on order** — Orders don't decrement inventory quantities. Inventory is managed manually.
16. **Notification bell / read-all in admin** — Notifications are queried but the admin dashboard only shows an unread count KPI. There is no panel to actually view and mark notifications as read.
17. **Customer birthday capture** — `birthday` is in the `Customer` type and DB schema but nowhere in the UI does the customer enter their birthday.
18. **Saved addresses** — `saved_address` exists in the schema but is never used in any UI.
19. **Peak hour analytics** — README requires "Peak Ordering Hours" chart; Reports page only shows revenue KPIs and top sellers table. No time-of-day histogram.
20. **Sales graph / chart** — No charting library is installed (no Recharts, Chart.js, etc.). Reports has only text/table data.
21. **`/menu` route is a stub** — `src/routes/menu.tsx` is only 37 lines and just re-renders `<MenuExplorer />` with no `<SiteFooter />`. Contrast with the home page which wraps sections properly.

### Auth / Security gaps
22. **No RLS (Row Level Security) configuration** in code — There are no RLS policies defined in the codebase. If RLS is not configured on the Supabase project, the public Supabase client could read/write all tables.
23. **`session_token` exposure** — The order `session_token` (UUID) is passed as a URL search param `?t=`. If someone shares the URL it grants order access. Acceptable for MVP but should be noted.
24. **Admin role bootstrapping** — There is no seeding script or UI flow to insert the first `user_roles` row. The owner must manually insert their admin role into Supabase.
25. **Coupon code validation UX** — Coupon is accepted at the text input level but there is no "Apply" button with real-time feedback. Invalid coupons are silently ignored (no server-side error message for bad coupon codes in the current flow — the discount just applies as ₹0).

### Build / Runtime issues
26. **Tech conflict in README** — `README.md` says "DO NOT USE React" and "Use Vanilla JavaScript", but the project is built entirely in React + TypeScript. The README is the original Lovable prompt, not a specification for the current codebase.
27. **`og-image.jpg` missing** — Will result in broken OG preview on social media.
28. **No `AGENTS.md` instructions followed** — `AGENTS.md` exists (1694 bytes) but may contain stale or Lovable-specific guidance that no longer applies.
29. **`bun.lock` and `package-lock.json` both present** — Dual lockfiles indicate the project was started with Bun but may also need Node/npm compatibility. Can cause resolution conflicts if both are updated independently.

